<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="6">

  <DocumentRef DateTime="20261018T235602" id="e9033e68-0bc0-496e-accf-fb85c1d1ec6b"/>

  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="346106d3-13a8-489f-bbab-c94c68da2e87">
      <SceneProperties Length="3 3/8" Page="1" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="ba5033e5-c3ec-40c5-a617-550251fa3ccc"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MISS ADELE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="8a3d6a31-f413-47d4-bd58-e0b21aeded0b"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="47bfe5fc-9804-43c4-ba8d-a054657d9ba9"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. DOT'S DINER - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="799a18d9-0202-45cc-9fdb-0e945d0e36ca">
      <Text>Lunch thinned out. Two booths still working on pie. A ceiling fan that moves the smell of the grill around and nothing else.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="ca2dda4b-d468-4074-a90e-47d25087eb8d">
      <Text>Behind the counter, DOT </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">MABRY</Text>
      <Text>, 60s, flat-footed, forearms built by decades of handling trays. She pours before she's asked to.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="fad82d2b-36a0-48e8-9e45-8df20f55e9a5">
      <Text>In the back booth, RUCKER. Hat on the seat beside him. A file open. Cold cup of coffee in front of him. Dot tops it off without breaking his concentration.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="2cd34933-7c05-466f-849b-ef7d7c0b9de7">
      <Text>MERCER comes in, civilian clothes, a hospital bracelet still on his wrist, and stops inside the door the way a man does in a place he has never been. He spots Rucker. Crosses to the booth and stops a step short of it, hands at his sides.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a3a6d76b-f563-43c2-a666-bb454751b97e">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2257be7d-44af-41b8-b265-a07fd172db51">
      <Text>Marshal. Captain Sloan said I'd find you here.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="53289490-10a1-4397-92e7-74d0000183f7">
      <Text>Rucker turns a page.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0b4f7765-373a-4b77-aa8c-417784ea0551">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7db28128-76b7-4bd9-95aa-de5b8b2d0c60">
      <Text>Marshal.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="05f2a367-1242-4ee9-95fd-d0a7db800cfc">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ba2b17c3-5d68-4250-817f-052cdc94fadf">
      <Text>I heard you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="47827eeb-978c-431d-81b4-af6818d426d8">
      <Text>He reads to the end of something. Then his eyes come off the page as far as the hospital bracelet, and no farther.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="64a2abc9-1f04-4d9c-9211-d5119b7aebd4">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ba49f179-03c9-4dae-b106-f757c125b7d5">
      <Text>You're his </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">probie</Text>
      <Text>.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9465f6fa-5328-4993-a173-0eb6606b3f47">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bf0fbf66-3d76-42b2-bd65-c212c14b0bb4">
      <Text>Danny Mercer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e8897e80-7615-4545-b4b3-82f320a88445">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="94a085e9-4300-4a7e-a7af-1c89bc530f08">
      <Text>They tell me you kept your </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">facepiece</Text>
      <Text> sealed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b54a7aaf-78e8-4493-a424-001c7747f627">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="849c1824-0dd0-4591-8063-fe213e1e1807">
      <Text>Yes, sir. Academy said keep the seal. Better to go into arrest than breathe the room. That's what the -- my mama asked the nurse what arrest meant and the nurse said --</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="a494b2ec-9086-4c77-9178-bc71a63aeeb9">
      <Text>He stops, because that is not what he was asked.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f81e1b1f-15f6-4ec8-ad29-e2a70fbd5a9b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e6e05a50-f162-40bd-b880-0c90ff478b68">
      <Text>Said what.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="622f1585-074f-474f-b417-61ebe9a70f0b">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0fdc8a3e-184d-4a99-8830-1a64c4f1cdf9">
      <Text>Said it meant my heart stopped. She already knew that. She just wanted somebody to say it to her.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="4ac49998-a934-4f5d-b9a0-c5a9bef867cb">
      <Text>Rucker lets that go by. He says the next thing to the page.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="60db334b-6173-4c6d-b5ea-40de567d588e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e5f38cf8-0f50-4e99-97a0-345f042790dd">
      <Text>Well. That's why you're standing in Dot's and not laying out at Shady Grove.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="1e46a744-9a11-40d2-b26b-7a1af305a269">
      <Text>Mercer shifts his weight. He has nowhere to put his hands and leaves them where they are.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0ffddd10-0ab3-488d-a7c9-2b241cc67e7c">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="03e6b104-ce76-4a08-87a3-ef3697cf7f51">
      <Text>The ceiling in that building. Tell me the last thing it did before it came down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ca56367f-c1ba-4e5e-a617-101b37386b77">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="de67819e-f79a-4cc1-b9c6-8496bfa01e8c">
      <Text>It came down. It let go all at once --</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e7aa4a39-9f85-46d0-bfd6-75f1e83aae91">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="18549eb2-879f-40c5-b0b1-ede156ef4504">
      <Text>Before that.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="393e3250-df19-4ea3-bd76-ce116b7355a7">
      <Text>Rucker waits with his file. He doesn't look up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="6e493282-0b33-43f6-9967-ae8a0ea60ddf">
      <Text>Mercer looks at the table, not at him. At the cold cup.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="39405e1c-9f7c-4e36-84ff-72d4db02561d">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="859cfc92-a914-4c25-a2b4-413ada7fcc1f">
      <Text>It got quiet. Rolling and popping the whole way in, then it got quiet.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="1be400ba-cc0a-434d-965a-4ca47f507f4f">
      <Text>Rucker closes the file. Looks at Mercer for the first time. Pushes the chair out with his boot.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="524216d1-c6f6-49a8-9179-8e64ad4fa557">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7414f853-4b57-4f10-b73f-13777e80bb18">
      <Text>Fire in a void goes quiet right before it shows itself. You had four seconds of quiet. You spent them moving. Sit down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="54965b7f-2c05-4ef7-80c3-343780333486">
      <Text>Mercer sits on the front of the chair, sore, the bracelet arm held a little off the table. Dot passes with the pot. Without asking, she leaves a fresh cup beside Mercer. He starts to thank her. She's already at the next booth.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="afe150fa-03e3-4fe6-ab9e-7f565fb9eefe">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5bc74583-42e2-41c7-89b8-724cae2c49a6">
      <Text>They tell me you can't pull hose for six weeks.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d1b1cf6e-3b41-4174-a827-8af9607250c3">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="09107fd9-b8d3-40cb-8a85-c1ff01e9c46c">
      <Text>Doctor said six. Chief said we'll see.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fd7368d8-caa8-4539-b219-dcc49d84bb05">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cebded6b-d2b2-4b6b-a894-efb3e703b01b">
      <Text>They also tell me you lost the line and your captain had to put a Mayday out on you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="642753b1-8a96-43e2-b9fd-0e9fb30ac892">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="df7fd63d-bab3-4097-ac6c-4ff873e2fb51">
      <Text>Yes, sir.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="ec2cd3c1-30bb-433c-9c76-3a9abfc6d29a">
      <Text>Rucker lets that sit on him. Looks at the bracelet. At the file under his own hand. He does not like what he is about to do.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e60c075e-9cf8-4aa4-9549-4fc8393673f0">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="885aa503-333b-46e1-8c31-37eb2999b9f0">
      <Text>Can you carry a camera without losing it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b404e3fd-95cf-4823-b22f-b0ef91672701">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4ec07c51-77cc-40ae-b930-b4d709000356">
      <Text>Yes, sir.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ab08a5a6-4472-4fec-9391-b98abc7c140b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="84e14d29-721c-49bb-8a6a-47e74774dc8c">
      <Text>Then here's how it goes. You drive mine. You carry what I hand you. You don't touch anything I haven't pointed at. And the main thing, you listen twice as much as you talk. You start now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f0ab8abc-fd1d-4151-bd91-02a1af653d52">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="64186e51-e181-434b-a358-d3343d9ff883">
      <Text>Now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="c4dee073-b231-439a-ade6-9ab7152148c8">
      <Text>Rucker doesn't answer that. He slides the file across the table, turns it so it reads right side up to Mercer. Cedar Street photographs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="57ebfd08-5f5c-40f6-92b7-14bc557b958c">
      <Text>Mercer looks at the file, not at him. Puts a hand flat on the edge of it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="ab040bfb-476d-4304-aa5f-83f2c0e20a60">
      <Text>At the front, a check paid, a purse closed. MISS ADELE FANNIN, 80s, stops beside the booth on her way out, because it is his booth and she always does. One hand flat on the table, the other on her purse. She looks at the boy, and at the bracelet, a while.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ce605f1f-ed49-4c32-94a0-90d54e6223b4">
      <Text>MISS ADELE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1833bf4e-2105-4aeb-8e5b-1c2c1a42cfdc">
      <Text>This your boy, Eldon?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="eaea674c-b0d5-4b85-8a4b-c8e4da192406">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3be6fea7-ac65-49ae-aeaf-1b4964fa74c8">
      <Text>Sloan's.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cbfb7fd8-4d08-44ab-b13f-6f7bdeb8e517">
      <Text>MISS ADELE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="69879f59-5372-4fd5-8055-e99bba16faa1">
      <Text>Hm.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="0663de64-2341-485a-9f52-6767946ea2f4">
      <Text>She has decided something about him anyway. Then she looks at the file.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3d1fd0d4-523a-4323-b580-c66056c0a7a3">
      <Text>MISS ADELE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7440f539-a666-4324-9c71-7a238997fbfa">
      <Text>Eldon.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="bdeaa928-8dfc-4427-9e5a-829b2e376e19">
      <Text>Rucker looks at Mercer, not at her. Opens the Cedar Street file to the first photograph and turns it toward him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f19293ff-fb22-4ca2-ac54-ddeb5f354507">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="02729f5c-95c7-4023-9a42-0d000b4de014">
      <Text>Yes, ma'am.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="4a5a1106-2ef1-4678-91a1-f7d75d9c96e3">
      <Text>Miss Adele pats the table once and heads for the door. The bell jingles. Dot lifts the pot at her without stopping.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="e6a0756f-597f-4276-a63d-f2621700329a">
      <Text>Mercer studies the first photograph, then the next. The bracelet goes under the edge of the table.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="0843eb11-015d-445e-8ce6-55e31e0d145f">
      <Text>Rucker drinks the cold coffee and watches him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
  </Content>

